---
const days = Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, index) => index + 1);
---

<figure class="rolling-window" aria-labelledby="rolling-window-title">
  <figcaption>
    <span>Static mental model · seven-day example</span>
    <h3 id="rolling-window-title">The window moves forward with time</h3>
    <p>Compare the same retention setting on two consecutive days. Green days are inside the available recovery window.</p>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="window-comparison" role="img" aria-label="Today, days 2 through 8 are in the seven-day recovery window. One day later, days 3 through 9 are in the window. Day 2 leaves as day 9 enters.">
    <div class="window-state">
      <div class="state-heading"><span>Today</span><strong>Day 8 is “now”</strong></div>
      <ol class="window-track">
        {days.map((day) => (
          <li class:list={{ outside: day === 1, available: day >= 2 && day <= 8, future: day === 9, start: day === 2, end: day === 8 }}>
            <span>Day {day}</span>
            <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <small>{day === 1 ? 'aged out' : day === 9 ? 'not yet' : day === 8 ? 'latest' : 'available'}</small>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="window-shift" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>Day 2 leaves</span><i>→</i><strong>the seven-day window shifts</strong><i>→</i><span>Day 9 enters</span>
    </div>

    <div class="window-state">
      <div class="state-heading"><span>One day later</span><strong>Day 9 is “now”</strong></div>
      <ol class="window-track">
        {days.map((day) => (
          <li class:list={{ outside: day <= 2, available: day >= 3, entering: day === 9, start: day === 3, end: day === 9 }}>
            <span>Day {day}</span>
            <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <small>{day <= 2 ? day === 2 ? 'just left' : 'aged out' : day === 9 ? 'new latest' : 'available'}</small>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="window-takeaway">
    <strong>What changed?</strong>
    <p>The retention setting stayed at seven days. The boundary moved: the oldest day left the window as a new day entered it.</p>
  </div>
</figure>
